{"kind":"stack","id":"stk-states","title":"Changing state: heating and cooling materials","theme":{"background":"#f4f9ff","foreground":"#1a2b3c","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Melting"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Melting is when a solid turns into a liquid when it is heated."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Freezing"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Freezing is when a liquid turns into a solid when it is cooled."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"ice"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"At what temperature does pure water freeze?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"0 °C","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"10 °C","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"50 °C","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Chocolate melts when it is heated. What state is it in once melted?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Liquid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Gas","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Solid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Which change of state happens when a puddle dries up on a warm day?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Evaporation","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Freezing","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Dissolving","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You are making ice lollies. Do you put the juice in the freezer or leave it on the table?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Put it in the freezer","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Leave it on the table","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The juice cools down and slowly freezes into a solid lolly. Well done, you used cooling to change state!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"The juice stays runny and does not freeze. Cooling is what makes a liquid turn into a solid."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Wax in a candle melts when it is heated. What happens when the melted wax cools down?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"It turns back into a solid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"It turns into a gas","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"It disappears","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"A thermometer shows water at 100 °C. What is happening to the water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"It is boiling","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"It is freezing","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"It is melting","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the changing state quiz."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"You now know how heating and cooling change materials, and at what temperatures water freezes and boils."}],"actions":[]}}
